<title>ITALY: Berlusconi not ruling out talks on early 98 budget.</title>
<headline>Berlusconi not ruling out talks on early 98 budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian opposition leader Silvio Berlusconi said he was open to government proposals to bring forward the 1998 budget as long as it contained structural measures to cut social welfare spending.</p>
<p>Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi has said next year's budget could be approved as early as August 15 if all political forces agreed and that such a move would be a clear signal Italy wanted to be in the first wave of European Monetary Union.</p>
<p>The budget has to be drawn up by September 30 and passed into law by parliament by end-December.</p>
</text>
